# E0059: `print` or `eprint` of something it cannot print

`print` and `eprint` take exactly one argument, an `i64`, a `u8`, a `bool`, a `char` or a `string`, and write it on its own line: `print` to standard output, `eprint` to standard error. The message names the function that was called.

## Why

An object, an optional or a call that returns nothing has no one way to be printed. A program prints the fields or the payload it means, one `print` or `eprint` each.

## Broken

```sisu
class Point {
    x: i64
}

fn main() {
    let p = Point(x: 1)
    print(p)
}
```

## Fixed

```sisu
class Point {
    x: i64
}

fn main() {
    let p = Point(x: 1)
    print(p.x)
}
```

